cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use GIPPA, please cite it as below."
title: "GIPPA: genome integrated prokaryotic proteomics analysis"
type: software
abstract: >-
  GIPPA (genome integrated prokaryotic proteomics analysis) takes one assembled bacterial genome plus
  proteomics evidence and asks what genome context explains about which proteins are detected, and
  how abundant they are. It places peptides and proteins on the genome with its own error control,
  builds one gene table keyed by Bakta locus tags, tests genome context (regions, autocorrelation,
  abundance islands, operons, function, sequence determinants), calls REF/ALT residues and novel
  ORFs, and writes standard tables, plots and an HTML report.
authors:
  - family-names: Hoang
    given-names: Khoa
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/khoa-yelo/gippa"
version: 0.0.1
keywords:
  - "proteogenomics"
  - "bacteria"
  - "genome context"
  - "operons"
  - "target-decoy"
  - "Nextflow"
